From 03fbb9dd77306f27a9fd504d774ea803035c7c0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 15:45:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07544/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5820: close
 offline/live ACTION6 bounds gap in reproduce()

ARC-AGI-3 Generalization-Testing Floor task class 2 (reusable-primitive
hardening). The offline arcade never validated ACTION6 click coordinates
against the live API's own declared [0,63] bound (arcengine's ComplexAction
already has it as Field(ge=0,le=63) -- only wired into the live HTTP
handler). This is the exact root cause behind lf52's original L9 route
reproducing cleanly offline while 400-ing live, fixed reactively on
2026-07-17 but never fixed at the source. arc_solver_kit.reproduce() now
flags this class of gap for any future solve, additively (does not change
reproduced/reached_level semantics).

Real, non-mocked verification: 10 new unit tests against the actual lf52
offline env, plus a full corpus audit (scripts/arc_action6_bounds_audit.py)
replaying all 25 currently-banked live-submission trajectories through the
hardened gate -- 2468 ACTION6 clicks checked, 0 out-of-bounds, 0 replay
errors (after discovering and fixing that several adapters expect their own
internal label dialect rather than the standard JSON encoding).

